# Domains

Put each business feature in `Domains/<Feature>/`, with stable namespaces independent of the generated host. A feature owns controllers, individual request/response records, validators, entities/configurations, optional services and its `IDomainModule` registration. MVC, validators and EF configurations are discovered automatically; the host discovers modules once.

Simple CRUD may inject repositories directly. Use services for reusable rules or orchestration. Cross-slice dependencies use versioned contracts, never implementation types. Runtime host code must not reference business implementations. EF-generated migration metadata is an intentional exception.

Read [Portability.md](../../../DeveloperReference/Portability.md) for the complete contract, routing, dependency, configuration and safe database upgrade policy. Read [TenancyQuickStart.md](../../../DeveloperReference/TenancyQuickStart.md) before storing tenant data.
